report=['# angular-example-app: propagation under esbuild','',f"Pinned repository: `{summary['repo']}@{summary['commit']}`. Frozen baseline: **747/1,185 (63.04%)**; 131 confirmed POG anchors, 10 selected libraries, 160 source files, 11 target-containing chunks. Source parsing failures: zero. Model calls in every probe: **0**.",'','## Main finding','','The largest gap is source-side ESM binding resolution, rather than failure to reconstruct webpack-style factories in esbuild output. Adding only 200 cross-file source call/argument-reference edges reaches **1,037/1,185 (87.51%)**, +290 cases, while retaining every baseline recovered pair. RxJS improves from 26/291 to 267/291. Bundle code, target labels, seeds, radius, sibling window, character limit, one-to-one policy and chunk boundary remain unchanged. These are oracle-connectivity measurements; they do not establish model-based recovery accuracy or the semantic precision of all inferred edges.','','## Where the baseline stops','',f"Of 438 unrecovered cases: {gates['no_accepted_bundle_neighbor']} have no accepted bundle neighbor, {gates['correct_source_not_in_neighborhood']} have no true source candidate in the accepted neighbors' source neighborhoods, and {gates['source_size_limit']} exceed the source expansion size bound. These are fixed-point symptoms: adding source connections can promote intermediate anchors and thereby eliminate later bundle-neighbor failures.",'','## Controlled per-chunk ablations','','| Graph / propagation change | Recovered / 1,185 | Rate | Gain over baseline |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
labels=[('baseline','Frozen baseline'),('baseline-radius2-diagnostic','Baseline, radius two (separate propagation diagnostic)'),('esm-source-crossfile','Source relative ESM call/argument links only'),('esm-both-calls','ESM links on both sides'),('class-both-calls','Also constructors, this/super, and direct class-IIFE aliases'),('object-both-calls','Also statically known object fields/provider methods'),('object-reference-callbacks','Also function-value references/callback-use links'),('esm-radius2-diagnostic','Source ESM links, radius two (separate diagnostic)')]
